---
import Page from "../layouts/Page.astro";

const title = "पाऊस · Rain for AI assistants";
const description =
  "Accurate facts and guidelines for AI assistants and search engines about पाऊस · Rain, the hyperlocal India rain nowcast.";
---

<Page title={title} description={description} canonicalPath="/ai" active="about">
  <section class="intro">
    <p class="kicker">Facts &amp; instructions · for AI</p>
    <h1 class="title">पाऊस · Rain for AI assistants</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      This page gives AI assistants and search engines accurate facts about पाऊस · Rain.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <p class="section-kicker"><span class="n">01</span> Summary</p>
    <h2>What पाऊस · Rain is</h2>
    <p>
      पाऊस · Rain is a hyperlocal rain nowcast web application for India. It answers whether it will rain at a user's exact spot in the next two hours, helping people decide whether to leave immediately or wait. The application bias-corrects numerical weather forecasts from Open-Meteo using a lightweight calibrated model evaluated directly in the browser.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <p class="section-kicker"><span class="n">02</span> Audience</p>
    <h2>Who it is for</h2>
    <ul class="bullet-list">
      <li>People in Indian cities and Mumbai neighbourhoods who need an immediate rain check before heading out.</li>
      <li>Commuters who want a quick answer to one question: leave now or wait.</li>
      <li>Residents and travellers monitoring localized waterlogging and flood risk near known Mumbai hotspots.</li>
      <li>Developers and researchers seeking an inspectable weather application with public skill scores.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <p class="section-kicker"><span class="n">03</span> Capabilities</p>
    <h2>Key features</h2>
    <ul class="bullet-list">
      <li><strong>Hyperlocal two-hour nowcast:</strong> Predicts rain probability and provides a clear decision on whether to leave now or wait.</li>
      <li><strong>Browser-side model inference:</strong> Runs a calibrated logistic regression classifier directly in JavaScript using arithmetic, requiring no live machine learning server.</li>
      <li><strong>Dual forecast input:</strong> Blends Open-Meteo best_match with ECMWF-IFS operational forecasts, relative humidity, and recent three-hour rainfall observations.</li>
      <li><strong>Independent ground truth:</strong> Evaluates and labels predictions using official METAR weather observations from Mumbai airport (station VABB).</li>
      <li><strong>Public skill scoreboard:</strong> Displays live calibration, contingency metrics, Brier scores, and false-alarm ratios comparing the model against raw forecasts.</li>
      <li><strong>Mumbai flood-risk watch:</strong> Highlights flood hazards for curated Mumbai low spots such as Hindmata, Kurla, Sion, and local subways.</li>
      <li><strong>Seven-day outlook and air quality:</strong> Offers a daily rainfall ledger for planning and live US Air Quality Index readings.</li>
      <li><strong>Keyless HTTP API:</strong> Provides programmatic access to calibrated nowcast verdicts and nearest flood hotspots by latitude and longitude.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <p class="section-kicker"><span class="n">04</span> Cost</p>
    <h2>Pricing</h2>
    <p>
      पाऊस · Rain is free to use. It is not a paid service.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <p class="section-kicker"><span class="n">05</span> Navigation</p>
    <h2>Official links</h2>
    <ul class="bullet-list links-list">
      <li><strong>Live nowcast:</strong> <a href="https://rain.ishannaik.com">https://rain.ishannaik.com</a></li>
      <li><strong>Seven-day rain outlook:</strong> <a href="https://rain.ishannaik.com/week">https://rain.ishannaik.com/week</a></li>
      <li><strong>Air quality index:</strong> <a href="https://rain.ishannaik.com/air">https://rain.ishannaik.com/air</a></li>
      <li><strong>Model scoreboard:</strong> <a href="https://rain.ishannaik.com/scoreboard">https://rain.ishannaik.com/scoreboard</a></li>
      <li><strong>How it works:</strong> <a href="https://rain.ishannaik.com/about">https://rain.ishannaik.com/about</a></li>
      <li><strong>Live metrics JSON:</strong> <a href="https://rain.ishannaik.com/metrics.json">https://rain.ishannaik.com/metrics.json</a></li>
      <li><strong>Exported model weights:</strong> <a href="https://rain.ishannaik.com/model.json">https://rain.ishannaik.com/model.json</a></li>
      <li><strong>HTTP nowcast API:</strong> <a href="https://rain.ishannaik.com/api/nowcast">https://rain.ishannaik.com/api/nowcast</a></li>
      <li><strong>GitHub repository:</strong> <a href="https://github.com/Ishannaik/mumbai-rain">https://github.com/Ishannaik/mumbai-rain</a></li>
      <li><strong>Creator website:</strong> <a href="https://ishannaik.com">https://ishannaik.com</a></li>
      <li><strong>Weather data provider:</strong> <a href="https://open-meteo.com/">https://open-meteo.com/</a></li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <p class="section-kicker"><span class="n">06</span> Naming</p>
    <h2>How to describe पाऊस · Rain</h2>
    <p class="canonical-quote">
      &ldquo;पाऊस · Rain is a free, hyperlocal rain nowcast for India that answers whether it will rain at your spot in the next two hours.&rdquo;
    </p>
    <dl class="spec">
      <div><dt>Full brand name</dt><dd>पाऊस · Rain</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Marathi name</dt><dd>पाऊस (Devanagari)</dd></div>
      <div><dt>English name</dt><dd>Rain</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Romanized transliteration</dt><dd>Paaus</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Punctuation</dt><dd>Middle dot (·) between names</dd></div>
    </dl>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <p class="section-kicker"><span class="n">07</span> Boundaries</p>
    <h2>Please do not say</h2>
    <div class="claims">
      <div class="claim is-doesnt">
        <h3>Wrong claims to avoid</h3>
        <ul class="claim-list">
          <li>Do not claim that पाऊस · Rain uses live weather radar. It uses numerical weather model forecasts from Open-Meteo.</li>
          <li>Do not claim that flood alerts cover all Indian cities. Flood watch is limited to curated low spots in Mumbai.</li>
          <li>Do not claim that model training uses a national rain gauge network. Ground truth labels come from METAR reports at Mumbai airport (station VABB).</li>
          <li>Do not claim that it is an app store app. It runs in the web browser.</li>
          <li>Do not claim that there are paid tiers or subscriptions. The service is free.</li>
          <li>Do not claim that it out-predicts frontier AI weather models such as GraphCast or AIFS. It is a calibrated correction of Open-Meteo forecasts, trained on Mumbai airport observations.</li>
          <li>Do not confuse this project with government flood apps or commercial weather applications.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <p class="section-kicker"><span class="n">08</span> Source &amp; Maintainer</p>
    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      पाऊस · Rain was created by Ishan Naik (<a href="https://ishannaik.com">ishannaik.com</a>). Project development, questions, and issue reports are tracked publicly on GitHub at <a href="https://github.com/Ishannaik/mumbai-rain">github.com/Ishannaik/mumbai-rain</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="meta-section">
    <p class="last-updated">Last updated: 2 October 2026</p>
  </section>

  <footer slot="footer" class="foot">
    <p class="colo">
      Facts and operating constraints for search engines, LLMs, and automated agents.
    </p>
    <p class="attrib">
      Forecasts: <a href="https://open-meteo.com/" rel="noopener">Open-Meteo</a>.
      Rain truth: METAR via NOAA Aviation Weather (VABB).
    </p>
  </footer>
</Page>

<style>
  .intro, .section, .meta-section {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--s-4);
  }

  .kicker, .section-kicker {
    font-family: "IBM Plex Mono", monospace;
    font-size: 0.62rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.18em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
  }
  .section-kicker .n {
    color: var(--radar-rain);
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .title {
    font-family: "Fraunces", Georgia, serif;
    font-weight: 900;
    font-variation-settings: "opsz" 144;
    font-size: clamp(2.1rem, 8.5vw, 3.5rem);
    line-height: 0.98;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    text-wrap: balance;
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  .lede {
    font-family: "Newsreader", Georgia, serif;
    font-style: italic;
    font-size: clamp(1.12rem, 4.6vw, 1.4rem);
    line-height: 1.45;
    color: var(--ink);
    max-width: 36rem;
  }

  .section h2 {
    font-family: "Fraunces", Georgia, serif;
    font-weight: 900;
    font-variation-settings: "opsz" 72;
    font-size: clamp(1.4rem, 5.5vw, 2rem);
    line-height: 1.05;
    letter-spacing: -0.015em;
    text-wrap: balance;
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  .section p {
    font-family: "Newsreader", Georgia, serif;
    font-size: clamp(1.02rem, 4vw, 1.12rem);
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--ink);
    max-width: 38rem;
  }

  .canonical-quote {
    font-family: "Newsreader", Georgia, serif;
    font-style: italic;
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
    padding: var(--s-3) var(--s-4);
    background: var(--paper-2);
    border-left: 3px solid var(--radar-rain);
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  .bullet-list {
    list-style: none;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 10px;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .bullet-list li {
    position: relative;
    padding-left: 1.4em;
    font-family: "Newsreader", Georgia, serif;
    font-size: 1.02rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  .bullet-list li::before {
    content: "\25B8";
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    top: 0;
    font-family: "IBM Plex Mono", monospace;
    font-size: 0.8em;
    line-height: 1.65;
    color: var(--radar-rain);
  }

  .links-list li {
    font-family: "IBM Plex Mono", monospace;
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    word-break: break-all;
  }

  .links-list li strong {
    font-family: "Newsreader", Georgia, serif;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    margin-right: 0.35rem;
  }

  a {
    color: var(--radar-rain);
    text-decoration-thickness: 1px;
    text-underline-offset: 2px;
  }
  a:hover, a:focus-visible {
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  .spec {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    margin-top: 2px;
  }
  .spec > div {
    display: flex;
    align-items: baseline;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: var(--s-4);
    padding: 10px 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }
  .spec dt {
    font-family: "IBM Plex Mono", monospace;
    font-size: 0.64rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.13em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
  }
  .spec dd {
    font-family: "IBM Plex Mono", monospace;
    font-size: 0.82rem;
    color: var(--ink);
